course: dictionary
lesson: 14597
title: Plush: soft and luxurious
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Plush can be an adjective or a noun, and the sentence tells you which one. «The hotel lobby was plush, with thick red carpets and gold lamps.» Here plush describes the lobby. It means rich, comfortable and expensive-looking. Ask yourself: is the word describing something, or naming a thing?
explain: «The seats were covered in a soft, plush fabric.» Now plush names the material: a soft fabric with a thick, furry surface. Words like soft and covered are clues that plush is a noun here.
explain: Look at the words around plush for clues. Gold, carpets and velvet point to luxury. Soft, furry and hugged point to toys. «Ella hugged her plush rabbit before bed.» The word hugged is a clue that a plush toy is a soft cuddly toy.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Plush» means rich, comfortable and expensive-looking, as in «a plush hotel».
fact: «Plush» can also be a noun: a soft fabric with a thick, furry surface.
fact: A «plush toy», or «plushie», is a soft cuddly toy.
exercise: «The king sat on a plush red chair.» What does plush mean here? | *Rich and comfortable | Very cold | Dirty and broken | Thin and light
exercise: «Mum bought me a plush toy for my little sister.» What is a plush toy? | *A soft cuddly toy | A type of car | A metal robot | A loud drum
exercise: «The cushions were covered in soft plush.» What kind of word is plush in this sentence? | Verb | Adverb | Adjective | *Noun
test: «The plush carpet felt warm under our bare feet.» What does plush mean here? | Wet and muddy | Rough and cold | *Thick, soft and luxurious | Very small
test: «Sam hugged his plushie all night.» What is a plushie? | A type of rain | A pair of shoes | A kind of food | *A soft cuddly toy
exam: «The room was plush, with velvet curtains and deep armchairs.» Which meaning fits plush best? | *Luxurious and comfortable | Cold and empty | Dusty and old | Noisy and crowded
